---
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import RepairPdf from '../islands/RepairPdf';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What kinds of damage can be repaired?', a: 'Common problems like a broken or missing cross-reference table, a cut-off end of file from an interrupted download, or wrong internal offsets. Pages whose actual content was lost can’t be brought back.' },
  { q: 'Will repair change my PDF’s quality?', a: 'The first method is lossless: it rebuilds the file’s structure without touching content. Only if that fails does PDFSherpa rewrite the file with Ghostscript, which also keeps images at full quality.' },
  { q: 'Can it repair password-protected PDFs?', a: 'No. Repair never changes protected files. If you know the password, unlock the file first with <a href="/unlock-pdf">Unlock PDF</a>.' },
  { q: 'My PDF still won’t open after repair. What now?', a: 'The data is probably truncated or overwritten. Download the file again from the original email or website, or export it again from the program that created it.' },
  { q: 'Is my PDF uploaded?', a: 'No. Repair runs entirely in your browser, so even damaged confidential files stay on your device.' },
];
---
<ToolLayout
  slug="repair-pdf"
  title="Repair PDF – Fix Damaged or Corrupted PDF Free | PDFSherpa"
  description="Fix PDFs that won’t open, show errors or have missing pages. Lossless rebuild first, deep recovery second. Free and private: no upload."
  h1="Repair PDF"
  lead="Fix a PDF that won’t open, shows an error or seems to be missing pages. PDFSherpa rebuilds its structure losslessly and, if needed, recovers content, all on your device."
  howToTitle="How to Repair a PDF"
  steps={['Select or drop the damaged PDF.', 'PDFSherpa checks it and tries a lossless rebuild, then a deep recovery.', 'Download the repaired file and check its pages.']}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={['compress-pdf', 'merge-pdf', 'split-pdf', 'pdf-to-text']}
>
  <RepairPdf client:load />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>What Repair PDF does</h2>
    <p>
      PDFs get damaged when a download is interrupted, an email attachment is corrupted, or a program crashes while saving. Often the content is still
      there, but the file’s index (the cross-reference table that tells readers where each page lives) is broken. Repair PDF rebuilds that index so the
      document opens again.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check:</strong> PDFSherpa tests how many pages currently open.</li>
      <li><strong>Lossless rebuild:</strong> the file is re-read leniently and written out with a fresh, correct structure, without touching content.</li>
      <li><strong>Deep recovery:</strong> if that isn’t enough, Ghostscript reads whatever it can recover and writes a clean new PDF.</li>
      <li><strong>Verify:</strong> the result is opened again before you download it, and the number of recovered pages is shown.</li>
    </ol>

    <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="tool-article" />

    <h2>Common error messages this helps with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>“There was an error opening this document. The file is damaged and could not be repaired.”</li>
      <li>“Failed to load PDF document.”</li>
      <li>Blank pages, or a viewer that shows fewer pages than expected.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Avoiding damaged PDFs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Wait for downloads to finish completely before opening or moving the file.</li>
      <li>Avoid editing the same PDF in two apps at once, or saving to a USB drive that’s removed too early.</li>
      <li>Keep a backup of important documents in cloud storage or email.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>
      Repair can’t invent data that’s missing. If half the file never downloaded, those pages are gone, so download it again. Protected PDFs are never
      modified. Recovered files may lose interactive features like form fields or links when deep recovery is used.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>Damaged files are often important ones. PDFSherpa repairs them locally in your browser, and nothing is uploaded.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
